      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ELEVENTH SCOTCH (1) was quickly into stride and found the front last start to record an all-the-way win (22.53) at Warrnambool in a Bottom Up - Grade 5 over 390m. Winner at his latest appearance in one of the quickest times on the card. Can continue the winning form. NEW SHERIFF (4) was prominent throughout when winning two back but could manage only midfield last time when 4th and beaten 5.5 lengths at this track (24.56). Is yet to miss the placings from this draw, including three wins, from five starts. Has ability and can measure up. JULY SHE LIED (7) is a talented dog who is a winner of 19 races but missed the frame last time when fourth at Traralgon (24.34). Leading chance. BORROLOOLA BOY (6) is building a nice sequence of placings and will be thereabouts again.",
